The solution is correct. However, there's a bit of an overcomplication in applying the Binomial Theorem directly and then considering only the last two terms. A simpler approach would be to use the binomial expansion with only these last two terms from the start: \begin{align*}
(300 + 1)^4 &= (300)^4 + 4(300)^3(1) + 6(300)^2(1)^2 + 4(300)(1)^3 + 1^4 \\
&= 10^{8} + 0 + 0 + 1200 + 1
\end{align*}
